<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_19_2" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_19_2" name="19.2 Decommission and remove assets from service" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>19.2.1, 19.2.2, 19.2.3, 19.2.5 and 19.2.6 are drawn. 19.2.4 is a decision and has its own table.

THIS IS NOT 18.5. The asset is not coming back, and 19.2.2 says so in its own activity list. An isolation for planned work ends in 18.5.3 reversing the switching; an isolation for decommissioning ends in a physical end-state that 18.5 has no route to. Same clearance from 18.4.4, opposite destination.

The purge branch is commodity-split and the electric side is drawn as an absence rather than as an equivalent. 49 CFR 192.629 governs purging a pipeline; there is no federal purge rule for electric plant because there is nothing to purge. 192.727(b) also allows a small enough volume to be abandoned without purging, which is drawn as its own path rather than as a footnote.

Neither end of this group edits a register. 19.2.5 hands disposition evidence to 12.1.6 and 19.2.6 hands as-left connectivity to 12.2.3. The asset register and the spatial model are 12.0's to change.</documentation>
    <laneSet id="P_19_2_lanes">
      <lane id="l_192_am" name="Asset management">
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_start</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_conf</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_dec</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_rec</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_npms</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_file</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_hand</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_conn</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_pub</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_end</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="l_192_ops" name="Network operations and field">
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_req</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_clr</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_gw</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_pv</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_purge</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_elec</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_192_safe</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <startEvent id="n_192_start" name="A solution or a 17.3.5 clock requires removal"><messageEventDefinition id="n_192_start_md"/></startEvent>
    <userTask id="n_192_conf" name="Confirm asset identity and the reason it is leaving"><documentation>19.2.1. Including the 17.3 classification, because 19.2.4 needs to know which rule applies before anything is cut.</documentation></userTask>
    <sendTask id="n_192_req" name="Request isolation from 18.2"><documentation>19.2.2.</documentation></sendTask>
    <receiveTask id="n_192_clr" name="Receive the clearance 18.4.4 issues"><documentation>19.2.2. Received, never issued.</documentation></receiveTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_192_gw" name="Commodity"/>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_192_pv" name="Purge required"><documentation>19.2.3. 192.727(b) does not require a purge where the volume is small enough.</documentation></exclusiveGateway>
    <serviceTask id="n_192_purge" name="Purge under 49 CFR 192.629, then seal"><documentation>19.2.3, gas. The same 192.629 procedure as 18.4.3 and 8.6, on a different trigger.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_192_elec" name="Complete isolation under 1910.269(m)"><documentation>19.2.3, electric. No federal purge rule exists and none is implied.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <userTask id="n_192_safe" name="Prove it is safe to cut or seal"><documentation>19.2.3.</documentation></userTask>
    <businessRuleTask id="n_192_dec" name="Remove, abandon in place, or leave inactive (19.2.4)"><documentation>19.2.4. Returns the end-state AND the subdivision that authorised it.</documentation></businessRuleTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_192_rec" name="Record what was removed, sealed, filled or left"><documentation>19.2.5. With residual risk where plant is abandoned in place.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_192_npms" name="Waterway or offshore"/>
    <sendTask id="n_192_file" name="File under 49 CFR 192.727(g)"><documentation>19.2.5.</documentation></sendTask>
    <sendTask id="n_192_hand" name="Hand the evidence to 12.1.6"><documentation>19.2.5. Hand. 12.1.6 end-dates the register; this process does not.</documentation></sendTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_192_conn" name="Record the as-left connectivity and isolation points"><documentation>19.2.6. Abandoned plant stays on the map, marked abandoned.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <sendTask id="n_192_pub" name="Hand the as-left to 12.2.3 to publish"><documentation>19.2.6.</documentation></sendTask>
    <endEvent id="n_192_end" name="Asset out of service, disposition recorded"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_start_n_192_conf" sourceRef="n_192_start" targetRef="n_192_conf" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_conf_n_192_req" sourceRef="n_192_conf" targetRef="n_192_req" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_req_n_192_clr" sourceRef="n_192_req" targetRef="n_192_clr" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_clr_n_192_gw" sourceRef="n_192_clr" targetRef="n_192_gw" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_gw_n_192_pv" sourceRef="n_192_gw" targetRef="n_192_pv" name="gas"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[commodity = "gas"]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_gw_n_192_elec" sourceRef="n_192_gw" targetRef="n_192_elec" name="electric"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[commodity = "electric"]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_pv_n_192_purge" sourceRef="n_192_pv" targetRef="n_192_purge" name="purge required"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_purge_n_192_safe" sourceRef="n_192_purge" targetRef="n_192_safe" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_pv_n_192_safe" sourceRef="n_192_pv" targetRef="n_192_safe" name="volume small enough, 192.727(b)"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_elec_n_192_safe" sourceRef="n_192_elec" targetRef="n_192_safe" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_safe_n_192_dec" sourceRef="n_192_safe" targetRef="n_192_dec" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_dec_n_192_rec" sourceRef="n_192_dec" targetRef="n_192_rec" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_rec_n_192_npms" sourceRef="n_192_rec" targetRef="n_192_npms" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_npms_n_192_file" sourceRef="n_192_npms" targetRef="n_192_file" name="waterway or offshore"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[npmsFiling = true]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_file_n_192_hand" sourceRef="n_192_file" targetRef="n_192_hand" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_npms_n_192_hand" sourceRef="n_192_npms" targetRef="n_192_hand" name="neither"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_hand_n_192_conn" sourceRef="n_192_hand" targetRef="n_192_conn" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_conn_n_192_pub" sourceRef="n_192_conn" targetRef="n_192_pub" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_192_pub_n_192_end" sourceRef="n_192_pub" targetRef="n_192_end" name=""/>
  </process>
